# Cross-agent continuity

This repository is the shared source of truth for Cursor Local, Cursor Cloud, Codex, Claude Code, Cowork, and future agents.

## Before substantial work

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, `RULES.md`, `.ai/HANDOFF.md`, `.ai/ACTIVE_WORK.md`.
2. Inspect git branch/status/diff; preserve unrelated work.
3. For codebase questions, run `graphify query "<question>"` before broad exploration when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists.
4. Verify the actual source files before editing.
5. Read `.ai/DECISIONS.md` only for architecture, security, API, data-model, deployment, or workflow decisions.

## After relevant changes

Relevant = source, tests, schemas, migrations, dependencies, build/CI, runtime config, deployment/product behavior.

1. Run appropriate verification.
2. Run `graphify update .`.
3. Update `.ai/HANDOFF.md` (concise, replace stale info, <800 words) before the final response.
4. Update `.ai/ACTIVE_WORK.md` with task/branch/commit/status/continuation point.
5. Update `.ai/PROJECT_STATE.md` only for stable capability/limitation changes.
6. Update `.ai/DECISIONS.md` only for durable decisions.
7. Commit app + continuity + needed Graphify artifacts together; push the working branch.

## Do not

- Update continuity files for read-only conversations.
- Commit secrets, tokens, credentials, private env values, or production data.
- Deploy automatically.
- Force-push, delete branches, or overwrite protected `main` history without explicit approval.
- Load all of `graph.json` / `graph.html` into context.
